⚡🇮🇷🌊 Bloomberg reports that several European governments now believe some form of transit fees for commercial shipping through the Strait of Hormuz are becoming unavoidable, as negotiations continue over the waterway's future.

According to the report, European officials are increasingly viewing a compromise involving navigation or service fees as the most realistic outcome, rather than a return to the pre-conflict status quo.

